V4 (Loam UI Kit / v0-parity design system) complete.

Task: Loam UI Kit token linter (raw colours, >5 colours, >2 fonts, arbitrary px,
emoji icons, missing alt text, gradients) + `design_lint` agent tool.

Commits on khamis1992/v0-v4:
  17b288d feat(design): add Loam UI Kit token linter and design_lint tool (V4)
  da9d6c6 fix(design): exempt every declaration on a shared token-definition line (V4)

What was finished this session (continuing the interrupted one):
- Resolved the stale interrupted merge: a leftover MERGE_HEAD pointed at an
  unreachable commit, blocking commits. The merge resolution had already been
  committed as 17b288d, so the marker was removed (no work discarded).
- Root cause of the failing acceptance test
  (`minimalDesignLinter > scores a clean site 100 with no issues`): the token
  definition exemption only exempted a line declaring exactly ONE custom
  property, so a one-line `:root { --background: oklch(...); --font-sans: ...; }`
  had only its first token exempt and the rest flagged as raw colours.
  Fixed in src/design/tokenLint.ts by computing byte-offset ranges for every
  declaration on a token-definition line (lookbehind avoids `var(--x)` false
  positives; a declaration separator avoids `red --note` false positives) and
  reusing one `tokenRanges` array for the raw-colour rule, the palette counter
  and the summary colour count, so they cannot drift.
- Added three regression tests in src/design/__tests__/tokenLint.test.ts.

Tests (all pass from the worktree root):
  npx tsc --noEmit
  npm run build:server
  (cd packages/web && npx next build)
  node --import tsx --test src/design/__tests__/tokenLint.test.ts src/tools/__tests__/designLint.test.ts src/design/__tests__/evalDesign.test.ts
  -> 81 tests, 81 pass, 0 fail (15 acceptance fixture cases + linter + tool + eval)

